{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795617676,"nonce":"ylHBmB9RvNpALmUtAa64WBNcmW4=","title":"cn::code_editor: a wrapper with a floating find and replace toolbar, and the editor features we lack","message":"There is no cn code editor. blinc_layout has the engine (`widgets/code/`, `mod.rs` 3.2k lines, find bar in `search.rs`), and its find bar is a legacy overlay styled by `.blinc-find*` in UA_STYLES. This issue plans the cn wrapper, as the rich text editor (26002b4) was, and records what Ashui's `CodeEditor` and RayDE (an IDE on Ashui) have that Blinc lacks. Surveys were read-only; items marked \"reported\" were not run.\n\n\n`blinc_cn::components::code_editor(\u0026state, CodeEditorTheme)` wraps `blinc_layout::code_editor` with `search_enabled(false)`. It owns the find toolbar as an absolute child of a relative container, not an overlay, and drives `CodeEditorData`'s search fields directly. Classes are `cn-code-editor*` with rules in CN_STYLES (Sass later, see 831c99b). The layout editor keeps its own bar, since blinc_layout cannot depend on cn.\n\nFloating find and replace toolbar\n- Top right of the editor, flexing with its width; it wraps to two rows when narrow, or scrolls its controls as the rich text toolbar does. A fade and grow on open; the replace row reveals with a transition. A notch peak is not needed.\n- Built from cn components: a cn input for the query with Aa, ab and .* toggles inside it (icon buttons with tooltips and `aria-pressed`), a count (\"3 of 12\", \"No results\", a regex error in the danger colour), previous and next, close. Replace row: input, replace, replace all. New toggles: preserve case and find in selection.\n- Keys: Cmd or Ctrl+F opens it seeded from a single-line selection with the text selected; Esc closes and returns focus to the editor; Enter and Shift+Enter; Cmd+G; Alt+C, Alt+W and Alt+R toggle the options; Cmd+Alt+F or Ctrl+H opens the replace row; Cmd+Enter replaces all; Up and Down walk the query history.\n- Matches are marked in the text, and on the minimap and the scroll track; the current match has its own class.\n- Hooks: `.cn-code-editor-find`, `-find-field`, `-find-toggle`, `-find-count`, `-find-match`, `-find-match--current`; every look from CSS, tokens for colours.\n\nEngine prerequisites in blinc_layout\n- The defects in 0db5944 (`on_change` on replace, `$1` expansion, signal refresh, seeding).\n- A public `set_value` (node_editor_demo works around its absence), a read-only flag, a placeholder.\n- Multi-line search, find in selection, preserve case, search state as signals, match positions for the minimap, a way to focus the editor and the find field.\n- `tab_size` and `insert_spaces` (a fixed 4 spaces today), and undo that coalesces typing (one snapshot per character now, capped at 200).\n\n\nAshui has and Blinc lacks: triple-click line and shift-click extend; indentation after `{ [ :`, not only a copied indent; state kept across tab switches (folds, scroll, selection); programmatic edits as one undo step; remote peer carets; an app-driven completion popup (kind badge, detail, docs); hover hints with an emphasised signature; line action rows above lines; view zones between lines; gutter markers and change bars; a decoration API with squiggle variants; minimap marks; syntax state across lines and more languages (Haxe, JS and TS, Python, CSS); a read-only view; a diff viewer (`CodeDiff`).\n\nNeither has: multi-cursor and column selection; auto-close brackets and quotes and surround; comment toggle; move, duplicate, delete, join, sort and case change of lines; word wrap; whitespace rendering; rulers; sticky scroll; drag and drop of text; go to line and go to symbol; highlight of other occurrences; jump to bracket; find history; auto-triggered completion and signature help; a diagnostics panel; keyboard folding and indentation folds; inlay hints; semantic highlighting; snippets.\n\nRayDE's client surface, for the wrapper's provider hooks: completion with additional edits, hover, signature help, diagnostics, definition, type definition, implementation, references, document symbols, rename, formatting and workspace edits. It does not use code action, inlay hints, code lens, semantic tokens, document highlight, folding range or selection range.\n\nOutside an editor widget (an IDE layer, not this issue): tabs and splits, quick open, command palette, find in files, git gutter and Source Control, terminal, tasks, debugging, settings and key chords, themes, extensions, merge editor.\n\n0. The engine prerequisites and 0db5944, with tests.\n1. The wrapper, the floating find and replace, CN_STYLES rules, a demo, a book page, the component catalog entry (the website page) and previews.\n2. Editing essentials: auto-close and surround, comment toggle, line operations, triple click and shift-click, undo coalescing, keyboard folding, highlight of other occurrences, syntax state across lines, tab size.\n3. Language hooks on cn popovers: a completion popup, hover and signature help, a diagnostics list, gutter markers and change bars, go to line.\n4. Word wrap, sticky scroll, rulers, whitespace; then multi-cursor, inlay hints, code lens, semantic tokens, snippets, a diff view.\n\n- The wrapper edits, highlights, folds and shows the minimap as the layout editor does; find and replace works from the keyboard and the toolbar, narrow and wide.\n- Both CSS and a recorder test restyle the toolbar; modules stay under 1k lines; a demo, the book page and the catalog entry exist.","files":null}]}